# Go Style

## Error handling

Never use inline error checks. The `noinlineerr` linter enforces this.

```go
// BAD
if err := load(); err != nil {
    return err
}

// GOOD
err := load()
if err != nil {
    return err
}
```

Reference: `internal/dto/mapper.go`, `cmd/cron.go`

## Static errors

Use `errors.New()` for static messages. Use `fmt.Errorf` only when formatting values.

```go
// BAD
return fmt.Errorf("pipeline name is required")

// GOOD
return errors.New("pipeline name is required")
return fmt.Errorf("duplicate pipeline name: %s", name)
```

## Package naming

Use single-word package names without underscores: `runpipelines`, not `run_pipelines`.

## Imports

- Local prefix: `github.com/alexander-kolodka/crestic`
- Group imports: stdlib, third-party, local (goimports)

## nolint

Every `//nolint` directive must include an explanation.

```go
//nolint:gosec // G501: md5 used only for lock-file name fingerprint, not security
```

## Logging

Use `internal/logger` helpers. Do not use global loggers (sloglint enforces this).